    "result_text": "The build succeeds with all tests green.\n\n## Summary\n\nThe change adds a `displayName` field to owner responses, formatted as `LastName, FirstName`.\n\nThe endpoint (`POST /api/owners` \u2192 `GET /api/owners/{id}`) returns an `OwnerDto`, which is generated at build time from `src/main/resources/openapi.yml`. Two edits:\n\n1. **`src/main/resources/openapi.yml`** \u2014 added a read-only `displayName` string property to the `Owner` schema, so the generated `OwnerDto` gains the field.\n\n2. **`src/main/java/.../mapper/OwnerMapper.java`** \u2014 added a MapStruct `@Mapping` on `toOwnerDto` that computes `displayName` as `owner.getLastName() + \", \" + owner.getFirstName()` from the stored names.\n\nTest result: `Tests run: 1, Failures: 0, Errors: 0` \u2014 **BUILD SUCCESS**. The acceptance test `coreComputesDisplayName` (creates an owner with firstName `John`, then asserts `$.displayName` equals `\"<lastName>, John\"`) passes.",
